[Attached Table 2] <Amended July 26, 2017>

Schedule of Authorized Staff of the Commission (Related to Article 2(2))

<table>
<tr><td><strong>Total</strong></td><td>90</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>Political-service subtotal</strong></td><td>5</td></tr>
<tr><td>Chairperson</td><td>1</td></tr>
<tr><td>Vice-chairperson</td><td>1</td></tr>
<tr><td>Standing commissioners</td><td>3</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>General-service, special-service and specific-service subtotal</strong></td><td>85</td></tr>
<tr><td>Senior officials or special-service officials belonging to the Senior Executive Service</td><td>2</td></tr>
<tr><td>Deputy director general or secretary</td><td>1</td></tr>
<tr><td>Secretary, prosecutorial investigation secretary, technical secretary, or special-service official equivalent to Grade IV</td><td>8</td></tr>
<tr><td>Administrative officer, deputy audit officer, prosecutorial officer, investigation officer, social welfare officer, public health officer, maritime and fisheries officer, information systems officer, police superintendent, or special-service official equivalent to Grade V</td><td>23</td></tr>
<tr><td>Administrative senior officer, audit senior officer, prosecutorial senior officer, broadcasting and telecommunications senior officer, information systems senior officer, records researcher, social welfare senior officer, public health senior officer, maritime and fisheries senior officer, police senior inspector, or special-service official equivalent to Grade VI</td><td>23</td></tr>
<tr><td>Assistant administrative officer, assistant audit officer, assistant prosecutorial officer, assistant information systems officer, assistant disaster safety officer, assistant facilities officer, assistant social welfare officer, assistant public health officer, police inspector, or special-service official equivalent to Grade VII</td><td>24</td></tr>
<tr><td>Special-service official equivalent to Grade VIII</td><td>4</td></tr>
</table>

Notes

Of the authorized staff under this Table, the following positions shall be filled, respectively, by public officials belonging to the agencies specified:
- 1 person (1 senior official) from the Office for Government Policy Coordination or the Ministry of Strategy and Finance;
- 1 person (1 secretary) from the Office for Government Policy Coordination or the Ministry of Strategy and Finance;
- 3 persons (1 deputy audit officer, 1 audit senior officer and 1 assistant audit officer) from the Board of Audit and Inspection;
- 1 person (1 broadcasting and telecommunications senior officer) from the Korea Communications Commission;
- 1 person (1 administrative officer) from the Office for Government Policy Coordination;
- 2 persons (1 administrative officer and 1 assistant administrative officer) from the Ministry of Personnel Management;
- 3 persons (1 administrative officer, 1 administrative senior officer and 1 assistant administrative officer) from the Ministry of Strategy and Finance;
- 2 persons (1 administrative senior officer and 1 assistant administrative officer) from the Ministry of Education;
- 4 persons (1 prosecutorial investigation secretary, 1 prosecutorial officer or investigation officer, 1 prosecutorial senior officer and 1 assistant prosecutorial officer) from the Ministry of Justice;
- 7 persons (1 secretary or technical secretary, 2 administrative officers or information systems officers, 1 administrative senior officer, information systems senior officer or records researcher, and 3 assistant administrative officers, assistant information systems officers, assistant facilities officers or assistant disaster safety officers) from the Ministry of the Interior and Safety;
- 3 persons (1 administrative officer, social welfare officer or public health officer, 1 administrative senior officer, social welfare senior officer or public health senior officer, and 1 assistant administrative officer, assistant social welfare officer or assistant public health officer) from the Ministry of Health and Welfare;
- 4 persons (1 deputy director general or secretary, 2 administrative officers or maritime and fisheries officers, and 1 administrative senior officer or maritime and fisheries senior officer) from the Ministry of Oceans and Fisheries;
- 2 persons (1 police senior inspector and 1 police inspector) from the National Police Agency;
- 2 persons (1 police superintendent and 1 police senior inspector) from the Korea Coast Guard.
